[
  {
    "id": "AJC.picrep.divzero",
    "title": "Div-zero: the first DivFamily producer, and Div^0 representable by the terminal object",
    "status": "active",
    "owner": "pic-e",
    "summary": "Div0 vanishing SUBSTRATE landed (pic-e 0105 r3, commits 64348cf522/4f6a122ab9/52ba623e36 + docstring fix, DivFamilyZero.lean, all axiom-clean [propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound], lake env lean EXIT=0). New mathlib-absent reusable converses of isEmpty_schematicSupport_of_isZero: isZero_of_isEmpty (module on empty scheme is zero), isZero_of_isEmpty_schematicSupport (quasi-coherent + empty support => zero, via descent iso M=i_*i^*M), and the packaging iff isZero_iff_isEmpty_schematicSupport. The §5 producer ..._of_forall_isEmpty_schematicSupport is a RE-SPELLING not a reduction (work-reviewer I-1722): since x.F is quasicoherent, IsZero x.F / all-opens-subsingleton / empty-support are interderivable at every site. REMAINING (genuine, unchanged): HasFiberDeg 0 -> IsEmpty(schematicSupport x.F), needing the fibre-of-support vs support-of-fibre carrier bridge (reverse annihilator inclusion, absent) + degree-0-fibre => empty-fibre, both documented at DivSupportQuasiFinite.isFinite_support_of_fibers. Naive general-pi hz fails on the finrank junk value; a producer must gate on fibre finiteness. No new hypothesis."
  },
  {
    "id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.datum-tail",
    "title": "DD-R datum tail: universal family and DAT-D/DAT-G assembly",
    "status": "active",
    "owner": "ajcr-pic0-join",
    "summary": "After divRep, package the universal family and feed DAT-B/C/Q, finite-stage descent, gluing, and the final Pic^0 RepresentableBy datum. These consumers remain gated rather than parallel active work."
  },
  {
    "id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.divrep.parameter-decouple",
    "title": "Decouple curve genus from widened divisor degree",
    "status": "active",
    "owner": "ajcr-param-decouple",
    "summary": "REAL REMAINING REPRESENTABILITY JOIN. The rooted producer divFunctorAff_genus_representableBy represents divFunctorAff C (genus C). The unconditional Pic0 coverage theorem is indexed instead by admissibleCoverageParameter hpi (genus C), and genus_lt_admissibleCoverageParameter_of_ne_zero proves these parameters differ in positive genus. The current widened divisor-family and universal-window tower uses one Nat simultaneously for the curve Euler-characteristic normalization chi(O_C) = 1 - g and for the divisor-family degree/rank. Generalize that substrate to separate a curve-genus parameter gamma from a divisor-degree parameter n, recover the existing API on the diagonal n = gamma, then instantiate n = admissibleCoverageParameter hpi gamma and feed abelSigmaChartAff. No rational point, IsDivisorDegree genus, new certificate field, or assumed RepresentableBy witness is permitted."
  },
  {
    "id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.pic0-ring-effectivity",
    "title": "Ring-level plus-surjectivity from a module-finite representative (fact 1 core)",
    "status": "active",
    "owner": "pic-g",
    "summary": ""
  }
]

[
  {
    "id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.certificate.fibre-avoid",
    "title": "Fibre-avoid, infinite-field branch: twist finite divisor fibres into the two-chart overlap",
    "status": "done",
    "owner": "",
    "summary": "DONE FOR INFINITE k, commit c6a47016f. P1.exists_matrix_finite_subset_chartInter proves that one GL2 twist puts any finite subset of P1 inside the two twisted standard charts. DivSchemeCertZarFibreAvoid derives finite residue support from regular local equations on a smooth integral proper curve, maps that support into P1, chooses the twist, and spreads confinement over a Zariski neighbourhood by properness. The ThetaGeneratorSeed theorem is noncircular: its fibre_regular field supplies residue-pullback regularity before colength, projectivity, or certification is used. SCOPE LIMIT: every avoidance theorem that chooses two scalars assumes Infinite k. This row therefore closes exactly the infinite-field branch, not the arbitrary-field gate. The missing finite-field degree bound and finite-cardinality variant are tracked by finite-field-avoid."
  },
  {
    "id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.certificate.tube-fibre",
    "title": "Tube-fibre: at one base prime, put the family support of the pointwise seed system inside a single adaptation piece",
    "status": "rejected",
    "owner": "",
    "summary": "REJECTED 2026-07-25 (run 0048) — SUPERSEDED, not merely refuted-as-stated.\n\nThe goal (\"put the support inside a SINGLE adaptation piece\") was already refuted in run 0047 r6\n(not_exists_unique_support_piece, Picard/DivSchemeCertZarSep.lean:257). Run 0048 shows the intended\nreformulation (\"per-piece, for each j the fibre of the closure of the piece trace stays in the\npiece\") is EQUIVALENT to a statement with no pieces in it at all: the chart traces\nsupportLocus cap V_b must be closed in the relative curve\n(isClosed_supportLocus_inter_chart_of_forall_noLeak, Picard/DivSchemeCertZarChartTrace.lean). So\nthere is nothing left for this leaf to own; the obligation lives in chart-avoid and the production\nrule in chart-trace / swallow-adapt.\n\nWHAT SURVIVES AND IS STILL USED: exists_away_supportLocus_subset_of_fibre_subset and\nforall_noLeak_of_forall_supportLocus_subset (Picard/DivSchemeCertZarTube.lean) — spreading one-fibre\ncontainment in an OPEN to a basic-open base neighbourhood, and containment-to-hnoLeak. They are\nconsumed by swallow-adapt with U the swallowing piece.\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.fibre-koszul",
    "title": "DD-R fibre exactness: all-window field Koszul equality and normalized multiplication conjugacy",
    "status": "done",
    "owner": "",
    "summary": "LANDED. The divisor-window pencil gives the field multiplication-kernel equals Koszul-boundary theorem in every window, together with ambient normalization and multiplication conjugacy. This does not by itself provide all-stage relation-fibre models over residue primes."
  },
  {
    "id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.seed-fibre-models",
    "title": "DD-R seed fibre models: relation-image models at stages zero and one",
    "status": "done",
    "owner": "",
    "summary": "LANDED. DivSchemeHighWindowFibreModelBase proves the residue-prime relation-image models at stages zero and one, supplying the induction seeds. No all-stage fibre-model theorem is claimed here."
  }
]
